    <!-- Dedicated Invested-line color for the Portfolio Progression
         chart - deliberately NOT colorSecondary (teal #00897B), which
         sits close enough to colorGain (green #2E7D32) in hue that the
         two lines were hard to tell apart at a glance on a small phone
         screen, especially when the Value line is also green (gaining).
         A vivid blue has no hue overlap with green, red, or teal, so it
         stays visually distinct from the Value line regardless of
         whether that line is currently green (gain) or red (loss). -->
    <color name="colorProgressionInvested">#1E88E5</color>

    <!-- Fixed palette for chart slices, cycled if there are more slices
         than colors (now 14, not 7 - with a realistic 9-10 fund
         portfolio, 7 colors guaranteed repeats and made the legend
         genuinely ambiguous). Ordered so ADJACENT slices (which in
         practice are usually adjacent in the pie too, since slices are
         drawn in list order) jump hue meaningfully rather than sitting
         close together - green next to teal was a real problem: both
         sit in the same green-cyan hue range and nearly merged visually. -->
    <color name="chartSlice1">#2E7D32</color>
    <color name="chartSlice2">#1565C0</color>
    <color name="chartSlice3">#F9A825</color>
    <color name="chartSlice4">#8E24AA</color>
